#. ja: フェニックスの尾
#. de: Phönixfeder
#. fr: queue de phénix
#. column 2: tufts of phoenix down
#. column 8: The billowy plumage of the fledgling Phoenix─a legendary bird that, upon each fiery death, is said to rise from its own ashes in a literal “blaze of glory.” When placed within fifteen yalms of one who is incapacitated, it will instantly revive the person. While some cultures insist that the tailfeather's restorative properties trump those of down, these claims have yet to be proven in any sort of scientific capacity.<br><br>※Cannot be used during certain duties.
#. column 9: Phoenix Down
msgctxt "Item:4570:0:0"
msgid "tuft of phoenix down"
msgstr ""

